<p>NOTE: Net profitability for the first quarter was lower than the prior year quarter due primarily to a decline in the Company's gross margin.  The gross margin on the Company's own branded products improved (despite increases in dairy costs) and these higher margin Company brand products represented a greater proportion of net sales than in the first quarter of last year.  However, these margin improvements only partially offset the impact of lower margins on partner brand sales and the comparative benefit of a $2,100,000 reduction of cost of sales related to an insurance settlement recorded in the first quarter of 1996.</p>
